# The repl suites ARE the test suite, so they must be reviewable and their failures visible: in 2026-09,
# 220 of 410 were untracked under the blanket *.script rule above, which is how a failing suite
# (crash_yieldexpr, two stale assertions) stayed invisible, neither in git nor in any registry.
# The blanket rule still applies in the rest of the tree.
!assets/language/repl/**/*.slc

# ...and the SCRATCH tree: the one-off repros, print-only probes and older ad-hoc tests that used to sit in
# the gate directory (140 of them). They are NOT suites, so the gate does not run them, but they are kept
# TRACKED because this repository's records cite several by name and a repro nobody can read is not evidence.
!assets/language/scratch/**/*.slc

# ...and the HAND-RUN CORPUS (assets/language/misc), which used to be gitignored. It is the maintainer's own
# regression set, run by src/build/run-misc-scripts.sh: 120 scripts that caught three real defects in one
# afternoon (a Go-inspired delegate-name refusal, an Action`1`/`Action`2` arity bug among them). Evidence nobody
# can read is not evidence, so it is TRACKED now, grouped by topic, each group keeping its numbered order.
!assets/language/misc/**/*.slc
!assets/language/misc/**/*.inc

# ...and the COM samples, for a different reason: they are the EVIDENCE behind numbers this repository documents
# (docs/language/index.html quotes excel_vba_bench.script, excel_speed_bench.script and friends), and evidence
# nobody else can read is not evidence. Tracking them does NOT make them suites: SUITE_DIR is still the repl
# directory, so nothing here is run by the runner or seen by the checkers.
!assets/language/com/*.slc
# The bytecode tooling samples (bc_compile_run.script drives a child REPL over the
# dot commands), same reason as the com samples: the blanket *.script rule above
# keeps a tracked sample out of the index.
!assets/language/bc/*.slc

# ...and the DEV INSTRUMENTS (assets/language/probes/*.script), which used to live in tools/ as
# tools/probe-*.script. They moved because tools/ IS the MCP server's tool directory: the server EXECUTES
# every tools/*.script at startup, so a probe that blocks or breaks took the server down with it (measured:
# cdb-handles-probe.script's DebugBreak killed the process, control-behavior-probe.script hung it). They are
# still shipped next to the executable, under assets/, and still tracked here.
!assets/language/probes/*.slc

# ...and the UI tree (assets/language/ui/**): the demos a reader can run, the RAD designer's own work, the .ui
# sample data the designer loads, and the library files those demos import. Tracking them does not make them
# suites either: SUITE_DIR is still the repl directory, so the runner and the checkers never look here.
# What that tree PRODUCES stays ignored, named rather than by extension, so un-ignoring the sources cannot sweep
# an output in: the designer's "Gen code" button writes generated_form*.script, the *- Copie files are
# hand-made backups, and sample_uizz.ui is the designer's scratch model (a temporary file: the samples the
# self-test reads are sample_ui.ui and sample_uiz.ui). (*.7z, *.slcbc and *.log are already ignored above by
# extension.)
!assets/language/ui/**/*.slc
!assets/language/ui/**/*.ui
!assets/language/htmx/**/*.slc
!assets/language/htmx/**/*.ico
assets/language/ui/demos/generated_form*.slc
assets/language/ui/**/* - Copie.slc
assets/language/ui/demos/sample_uizz.ui

# Reasonix host config and session state, plus one stale artifact. None is used by the project: no code in
# src/, tools/ or assets/ reads them (only old plan docs mention the paths). reasonix.toml is the host's live
# config and .reasonix/ is its session state, which the tooling rewrites during a session, keeping them
# tracked made the working tree permanently dirty. They stay on disk; processed.xml was deleted as dead
# weight (17,889 lines, unchanged since the initial commit).
.reasonix/
reasonix.toml
processed.xml

# The VBA baseline workbook is generated: import assets/language/com/VbaBench.bas and save it as this file.
assets/language/com/VbaBench.xlsm
# Python bytecode, because the repo ships two runnable samples (bindings\BasicTest.py and bindings\BridgeTest.py) and
# running one writes this folder beside them, where it would otherwise sit untracked in every `git status`.
__pycache__/
# The C carrier's built exe: bindings\bridge_host.c is compiled in place by the command in its own header, and that
# build writes this one file beside it, so it is ignored rather than left untracked in every `git status`.
/bindings/bridge_host.exe
# Test artifacts a suite writes into the working directory. They are untracked by construction, so a gate run used
# to dirty the tree with files nobody wrote on purpose (json_test_temp.json and mydb.sqlite from the json and sqlite
# suites, xl_smoke_*.xlsx from the Excel smoke suites). Named specifically rather than by extension, so a real
# .json, .sqlite or .xlsx a person puts here is still visible to git.
/json_test_temp.json
/mydb.sqlite
/xl_smoke_*.xlsx
# The native resource compiler ILC runs leaves a Visual Studio .aps beside the launcher's .rc
*.aps
